{
  $schema: 'https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json',
  // No enabledManagers or branchPrefix here: each job in renovate.yaml sets
  // both in its global config, which this file would override. The job is what
  // gives each manager its cadence — monthly for the emulator images, weekly
  // for libraries-bom — and a manual recovery can run either on any day. The
  // branch prefixes must differ, because a run prunes every branch under its
  // prefix that it did not produce itself (ADR-0191).
  dependencyDashboard: false,
  automerge: false,
  draftPR: true,
  customManagers: [
    {
      customType: 'regex',
      managerFilePatterns: ['flink-connector-gcp-test-utils/**/*EmulatorContainers.java'],
      matchStrings: [
        'private static final (?:DockerImageName|String) IMAGE\\s*=\\s*(?:DockerImageName\\.parse\\(\\s*)?"(?<depName>(?:gcr\\.io|ghcr\\.io)/[^"\\s:]+):(?<currentValue>[^"\\s]+)"\\s*(?:\\)|;)',
      ],
      datasourceTemplate: 'docker',
      versioningTemplate: 'docker',
    },
  ],
  packageRules: [
    {
      matchManagers: ['custom.regex'],
      groupName: 'emulator images',
      groupSlug: 'emulator-images',
      separateMajorMinor: false,
      prBodyTemplate: '## WHAT\n\nUpdate the pinned emulator images used by the integration tests.\n\n{{{table}}}{{{warnings}}}\n\n## WHY\n\nKeep the pins current before registry retention removes an old image. The workflow runs monthly and can be dispatched manually for recovery.\n\nBefore merging, record the Bigtable deviation suites\' verdict and any changed behavior ([ADR-0044](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/adr/0044-the-e2e-suite-creates-an-ephemeral-bigtable-instance-per-gated-class.md)), and for the shared Cloud SDK image the Firestore rejection and BulkWriter defect suites\' verdicts (`FirestoreRejectionITCase`, `BulkWriterDefectsITCase`; [ADR-0171](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/adr/0171-the-firestore-sink-writes-through-bulkwriter-and-confirms-invalid-writes-alone.md)). For a Spanner bump, recheck the pinned-emulator measurements in [ADR-0075](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/adr/0075-the-spanner-sink-batch-writes-and-owns-the-whole-retry-loop.md) and [ADR-0077](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/adr/0077-batch-limits-are-counted-in-index-aware-cells-read-once-at-open.md). For Spanner or Cloud Tasks updates, update the matching `docker run` image tag in the [Spanner](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/content/docs/examples/spanner.md#running-against-the-emulator) or [Cloud Tasks](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/content/docs/examples/cloudtasks.md#running-against-the-emulator) example page; keep dated measurement references unchanged.\n\n{{{notes}}}{{{changelogs}}}{{{configDescription}}}{{{controls}}}{{{footer}}}',
    },
    // Dependabot owns every other Maven dependency; this manager proposes the
    // BOM alone (ADR-0191).
    {
      matchManagers: ['maven'],
      enabled: false,
    },
    {
      matchManagers: ['maven'],
      matchPackageNames: ['com.google.cloud:libraries-bom'],
      enabled: true,
      groupName: 'libraries-bom',
      groupSlug: 'libraries-bom',
      separateMajorMinor: false,
      prBodyTemplate: '## WHAT\n\nUpdate `com.google.cloud:libraries-bom`, which sets the version of every Google Cloud client library the connectors use.\n\n{{{table}}}{{{warnings}}}\n\n## WHY\n\nAdopt each BOM on `main` as it ships rather than once per release candidate ([ADR-0191](https://github.com/flink-gcp/flink-connector-gcp/blob/main/docs/adr/0191-libraries-bom-updates-are-proposed-weekly-by-renovate.md)). The workflow regenerates the shaded modules\' NOTICE files on this branch after Renovate pushes it; the rest of what a BOM bump owes stays with the reviewer:\n\n- Move `opentelemetry-bom.version` to the OpenTelemetry the new clients resolve; the `opentelemetry-upper-bound` enforcer execution names it when it fails (ADR-0186).\n- If the workflow\'s `bom_notices` job failed, the run pushed nothing, and this branch keeps whatever NOTICE files it last had; the job log names the cause. A licence text that no longer matches its pin in `scripts/config/licence-sources.toml` needs the new text reviewed and the pin updated, then `just update-notices`.\n- Add a relocation for any package root the packaging ITCase reports as unrelocated, then regenerate the NOTICE files with `just update-notices`.\n- Run the org.json check the root POM\'s comment prescribes.\n- Run the client-upgrade rechecks each module reference under `.agents/references/modules/` names, and re-read every documented claim about what a moved SDK does or lacks.\n- Re-measure the client-metrics instrument inventories the Bigtable, Spanner and Cloud Tasks pages document.\n\n{{{notes}}}{{{changelogs}}}{{{configDescription}}}{{{controls}}}{{{footer}}}',
    },
  ],
}
